      },
      "worked": "In $\\triangle AOB$, use the cosine rule:\n$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=3^2+4.5^2-2(3)(4.5)\\cos70^\\circ\\\\AB&=\\sqrt{29.25-27\\cos70^\\circ}\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$\nLet $E$ be the point on $BC$ level with $D$. Then $DE=AB$ and $CE=3-2=1\\text{ m}$. The angle of elevation is $\\theta=\\angle CDE$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{CE}{DE}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29.25-27\\cos70^\\circ}}\\\\\\theta&=\\tan^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29.25-27\\cos70^\\circ}}\\right)\\\\\\theta&\\approx12.6^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
